/-!
# Internal Hom preserves `Dctf`, by dévissage

For a field `k`, a finite ring `Λ` whose exponent is invertible on `k` and a scheme `X` of
finite type over `k`, the derived internal hom `RHom(K, L)` of two objects of `Dctf(X_ét, Λ)`
lies in `Dctf(X_ét, Λ)` (`AlgebraicGeometry.Etale.constructibleFiniteTor_derivedHom_of_field`,
blueprint `det-rem-sf-matrix-hom-devissage`).

The proof is a dévissage in the first variable. The objects `K` with `RHom(K, L) ∈ Dctf` form
a thick subcategory (`lem-sf-hom-triangulated`), and `Dctf(X, Λ)` is the thick subcategory
generated by the objects `Rg_* Rj_! P`, for `j : U ⟶ Ū` an open immersion, `g : Ū ⟶ X` a closed
immersion and `P` a lisse flat sheaf on `U`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Etale.ctf_generated_by_rightDerivedLowerStar_rightDerivedLowerShriek`).
For such a generator, the tensor–Hom exchange for `g` and for `j`
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Etale.derivedHomRightDerivedLowerShriekIsoOfFinite`, the instances of
blueprint `lem-weil-stratum-ambient-hom` used by the blueprint proof) gives
```
RHom(Rg_* Rj_! P, L) ≅ Rg_* RHom(Rj_! P, Rg^! L) ≅ Rg_* Rj_* RHom(P, Rj^! Rg^! L),
```
and `RHom(P, M) ≅ P^∨ ⊗ᴸ M` for the lisse flat, hence dualizable, sheaf `P`
(`lem-sf-hom-finite-projective`). Each of `Rg^!`, `Rj^!`, `P^∨ ⊗ᴸ -`, `Rj_*` and `Rg_*`
preserves `Dctf`.

## Implementation notes

The blueprint states the lemma over a separably closed field; the proof only uses the
stability of `Dctf` under `Rf_*` and `Rf^!`, which holds over any field
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Etale.constructibleFiniteTor_rightDerivedLowerStar`,
`AlgebraicGeometry.Etale.constructibleFiniteTor_rightDerivedUpperShriek`), so no hypothesis on
`k` is made. The blueprint proof runs the Noetherian induction itself, with a dense open on
which `K` is perfect; here that induction is the one inside the generation theorem.
-/

@[expose] public section

universe u

open CategoryTheory Limits MonoidalCategory Opposite ZeroObject Pretriangulated

open scoped CategoryTheory.Functor

namespace AlgebraicGeometry

open Scheme

namespace Etale

open _root_.AlgebraicGeometry.Etale.DerivedCategory

variable (Λ : Type (u + 1)) [CommRing Λ] [Finite Λ]

end Etale

end AlgebraicGeometry
